<p>WW Wood Products builds Shiloh, Eclipse, Aspect, and Vistora in Dudley, Missouri. Pinnacle Sales is the WW Wood dealer representative across Arizona, California, Colorado, Idaho, Montana, Nevada, New Mexico, Oregon, Utah, and Washington.</p>

<h2>WW Wood first</h2>
<p>Family-owned since 1977. <a href="/brands/shiloh-cabinetry/">Shiloh</a> is usually the first line: face-frame and inset, paint program, plywood box. <a href="/brands/eclipse-cabinetry/">Eclipse</a> is frameless from the same plant, same doors and finishes. <a href="/brands/aspect-cabinetry/">Aspect</a> is the value line. <a href="/brands/vistora-closets/">Vistora</a> is the closet system. All four come out of Dudley.</p>

<h2>Lead times</h2>
<p>Shiloh, Eclipse, Aspect, and Vistora typically ship in about six weeks. Your rep will confirm current production on the intro call.</p>

<h2>Coming to the factory</h2>
<p>We take dealers through Dudley. Fill out the form, then your territory rep picks a trip that fits. If you want a sense of the visit, Greenwood's factory story is in the <a href="/playbook/greenwood-kitchens-factory-visit/">Playbook</a>.</p>

<h2>Territory</h2>
<p>WW Wood is a 10-state Western map. Check Shiloh on the <a href="/become-a-dealer/">form</a>, or any of the six public brands. You do not have to take all six. Custom shops and dealers leaving a stock or semi-custom program can start at <a href="/guides/become-a-shiloh-dealer/">become a Shiloh dealer</a>. Territory notes: <a href="/guides/protected-dealer-territories/">protected dealer territories</a>.</p>

</AeoGuide>
